# Beads runtime state. The JSONL store and this repo's README are committed
# with the implementation; everything a running beads daemon writes is not.
#
# Fixes #11691. The two JSONL-era patterns below were the whole file, and beads
# has since moved to a Dolt-backed store — so eleven runtime files, including a
# CREDENTIAL, sat untracked and un-ignored in the repo root. Two problems, not
# one: permanent `??` noise in every `git status` (the #9599 untracked-dirt
# failure), and a credential one `git add -A` away from being committed by an
# RC-cut or worktree flow that stages blindly.
#
# Deliberately scoped per-entry rather than ignoring `.beads/` wholesale: the
# JSONL store and README ARE tracked, and a blanket ignore would silently stop
# tracking them the next time either changed.

# --- JSONL store bookkeeping (pre-Dolt, still emitted) ---
.issues.jsonl.lock
.issues.jsonl-*.tmp

# --- credential: never commit ---
.beads-credential-key

# --- daemon runtime files: pidfile, port, lock ---
# (worded to avoid the database-CLI invocation pattern that
#  test_repo_runtime_has_no_database_backed_task_cli_path scans for --
#  these are paths a separately-installed beads writes, not commands we run)
dolt-server.lock
dolt-server.pid
dolt-server.port

# --- database data directories ---
dolt/
embeddeddolt/
backup/

# --- per-worktree bookkeeping, meaningless on another machine ---
.local_version
last-touched
push-state.json
interactions.jsonl
